{
  "name": "s117-test-run-does-not-touch-quality-gate-state",
  "setup_files": {
    "package.json": "{\"name\": \"demo\"}\n",
    ".claude/commands.json": "{\"typecheck\": \"false\", \"test-file\": \"true {file}\"}",
    "src/calc.ts": "export const add = (a, b) => a + b;\n",
    "src/calc.test.ts": "test('add', () => {});\n"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "hook": ".claude/hooks/quality-gate.sh",
      "payload": {
        "session_id": "sess-a",
        "tool_name": "Edit",
        "tool_input": { "file_path": "{TMPROOT}/src/calc.test.ts" }
      },
      "expect": {
        "exit_code": 0,
        "state": [{ "file": ".hook-state/last_quality_gate.json", "field": "last_run_status", "equals": "failed" }]
      }
    },
    {
      "hook": ".claude/hooks/test-run.sh",
      "payload": {
        "session_id": "sess-a",
        "tool_name": "Edit",
        "tool_input": { "file_path": "{TMPROOT}/src/calc.ts" }
      },
      "expect": {
        "exit_code": 0,
        "file_contains": [
          { "file": ".hook-state/test-run-log.tsv", "substr": "sess-a\tsrc/calc.test.ts\tsrc/calc.ts\tpassed\t" }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "hook": ".claude/hooks/stop-gate.sh",
      "payload": { "session_id": "sess-a", "cwd": "{TMPROOT}" },
      "expect": {
        "exit_code": 2,
        "stderr_contains": ["src/calc.test.ts"]
      }
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TAN-7039. Why the test run keeps its own log: quality-gate.sh gates test files too (calc.test.ts is a .ts file) and gate-state keys one scope per path, so a passing test run recorded there would REPLACE the failing typecheck for the same path and the stop would read clean. Two states, and the gate's verdict still blocks."
}
